<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constantine IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 650–685</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Constantine IV Pogonatos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Constantine IV (c. 650–685) was Byzantine emperor from 668 to 685. His reign saw the repulse of the Arab attacks on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in the 670s and the Third Council of Constantinople of 680–681, which condemned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monothelitism">Monothelitism</a>. His campaign of 680 against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgars</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asparuh-of-bulgaria">Asparuh</a> ended in defeat, and the peace of 681 recognised the new Bulgarian state south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantine-iv.jpg" alt="Constantine IV" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Constantine_IV_mosaic.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
